    <bpmn:process id="W_W5497" name="W5497. POSH / Safe Spaces Compliance Program — CODI Committee, Statutory Investigation &amp; Reporting (RA 7877 / RA 11313)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Report/complaint of sexual harassment or gender-based sexual harassment (GBSH) — work-related superior/subordinate, peer-to-peer, client/customer-to-employee, or online conduct against an employee; (b) annual CODI constitution/reconstitution cycle; (c) policy or regulatory change
Frequency: Continuous intake; annual committee constitution and code re-publication; case-driven investigations. Formal cases: ~10–30/year chain-wide (benchmark range for a 6,918-employee multi-site retailer, understated by underreporting without a trusted channel)
Volume: All 6,918 employees across 205 sites + ~10–20% contingent workers (VS-98) are in scope; both laws apply to every BuildRight entity with 10+ employees (all 205 sites qualify). One CODI per legal entity (5), each supported by trained case handlers; awareness training reaches 100% of employees annually (~6,918 completions)
Owner: Labor Relations Director
Participants: CODI Chair &amp; Members (HR, supervisory, rank-and-file, union representative where a CBA unit exists), HR Manager, CHRO, Legal Counsel (VS-100), EAP Manager/OH Nurse (VS-83), IT Security (online-conduct evidence, VS-27), DOLE (reporting/jurisdictional interfaces)
Source: workflow W5497 — POSH / Safe Spaces Compliance Program — CODI Committee, Statutory Investigation &amp; Reporting (RA 7877 / RA 11313)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5497_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5497_Lane1" name="Labor Relations Director">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5497_Lane2" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5497_Lane3" name="CODI Chair">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5497_Lane4" name="CODI Members">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5497_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5497_Start6" name="(a) Report/complaint of sexual harassment or gender-based sexual harassment (GBSH) —…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task7" name="Annual CODI constitution per entity: chair + members representing management…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual CODI constitution per entity: chair + members representing management, supervisory, and rank-and-file levels (plus the union representative where a bargaining unit exists — links to VS-84.1), with at least one member of each gender; publish committee membership, reporting channels, and the anti-harassment code on notice boards, ESS portal, and store huddle boards (links to VS-103.2 W3339)
Responsible (R): Labor Relations Director / HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 3–5 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task8" name="Code of conduct maintenance: definitions under RA 7877 (authority/influence SH)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Code of conduct maintenance: definitions under RA 7877 (authority/influence SH) and RA 11313 (peer, client-to-employee, online GBSH — including customer conduct toward cashiers, promodisers, and service-desk staff), examples, sanctions matrix, confidentiality/gag-order obligations, and whistleblower protection; annual employee acknowledgment captured in HR records (per W51 pattern)
Responsible (R): Labor Relations Director / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task9" name="Multi-channel intake: in-person (any manager, HR, or CODI member), ESS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Multi-channel intake: in-person (any manager, HR, or CODI member), ESS confidential form, hotline, or sealed written report; acknowledge within 24 hours; apply interim measures (schedule/location adjustment of the *respondent*, not the complainant; preventive suspension per W2883 where warranted); enforce gag order on disclosure of identities
Responsible (R): HR Manager / CODI Chair
Accountable (A): Labor Relations Director
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task10" name="Jurisdiction &amp; classification: determine RA 7877 vs RA 11313 track; route…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Jurisdiction &amp; classification: determine RA 7877 vs RA 11313 track; route adjacent matters — general grievances (W2881), ethics/corruption (VS-119), criminal conduct to Legal (VS-100) and PNP, customer-safety violence (VS-159.3); confirm CODI jurisdiction and statutory investigation clock
Responsible (R): CODI Chair / Legal
Accountable (A): Labor Relations Director
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task11" name="Investigation: documentary and interview evidence (complainant, respondent…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Investigation: documentary and interview evidence (complainant, respondent, witnesses) with RA 10173 safeguards (VS-91); written interview summaries; preservation of online-conduct evidence (messages, screenshots, posts) with IT Security chain-of-custody (VS-27); target completion within the statutory period (≤30 days from formal complaint)
Responsible (R): CODI Members / Legal
Accountable (A): CODI Chair
Duration: 15–25 days/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task12" name="Hearing &amp; determination: both parties heard separately; CODI deliberates on…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Hearing &amp; determination: both parties heard separately; CODI deliberates on preponderance of evidence; written report with findings, aggravating/mitigating factors, and recommended sanction aligned to the sanctions matrix; served with due-process notices (2-notice rule per W2883/W2884)
Responsible (R): CODI Chair / Members
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task13" name="Decision implementation &amp; appeal: management implements sanction (reprimand to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Decision implementation &amp; appeal: management implements sanction (reprimand to dismissal), records in the disciplinary file; internal appeal per policy; Legal explains criminal/civil options to the complainant (VS-100); SENA referral if the matter ripens into a labor dispute (W2885)
Responsible (R): HR Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task14" name="Remediation &amp; non-retaliation monitoring: workplace restoration (transfers…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Remediation &amp; non-retaliation monitoring: workplace restoration (transfers, team reintegration), 6–12-month retaliation watch (assignments, ratings, schedules), EAP counseling for the complainant and affected witnesses (W2865), warning/supervision for substantiated-but-minor findings
Responsible (R): HR Manager / CODI Chair
Accountable (A): Labor Relations Director
Duration: 6–12 months/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task15" name="Statutory reporting &amp; records: DOLE reportorial/submission requirements as they…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Statutory reporting &amp; records: DOLE reportorial/submission requirements as they apply to harassment cases and committee operations; anonymized quarterly case statistics to the Audit Committee (W1721); confidential case files retained per VS-88 retention schedule in a restricted-access class separate from ordinary personnel files
Responsible (R): Labor Relations Director / Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5497_Task16" name="Annual program review: case analytics (types, locations, customer-vs-employee…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Annual program review: case analytics (types, locations, customer-vs-employee origin, cycle time), root-cause and hot-spot analysis with LP/VS-23 where patterns indicate risk, refresher-training refresh with W719, policy/code update, and awareness campaign reinforcement at town halls (W3340/W2890)
Responsible (R): Labor Relations Director / HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 3–5 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5497_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5497_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5497_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5497_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-482 (ensure controlled execution — Grievance Handling, Labor Dispute &amp; DOLE Conciliation (PA-84.2).)
Owner: Labor Relations Director</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
